==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|l|o}}

===Etymology===
From *lowna ("day, midday"). Cognates include Karelian {{term|lounat|lang=krl}}, Veps {{term|louna}}, Votic {{term|lõunat}}, Estonian {{term|lõuna|lang=et}}, and Udmurt {{term|lun|lang=udm}}. Permic cognates have the meaning "day", whereas Baltic-Finnic cognates denote the direction where the Sun is at midday or the meal eaten at midday.

The compass point meaning was clarified in the 19th century; in earlier text and dialects ''lounas'' may mean either south, southwest or southeast.<ref>{{cite book | last = Häkkinen | first = Kaisa | year = 2004 | title = Nykysuomen etymologinen sanakirja | publisher = WSOY | id = ISBN 951-0-27108-X }}</ref>

